# Ticket Execution Workflow

When the user gives you a ticket (e.g., "M1-008", "work on the mission service", "implement risk evaluator"):

## Step 1: Identify and Read

- Find the ticket in `docs/13-milestone-tickets-and-implementation-plan.md`
- Read the FULL ticket including all sections
- Confirm the ticket ID and scope with the user before proceeding

## Step 2: Context Loading

Read these files IN ORDER before writing any code:
1. Every file in the ticket's "Files to read before starting"
2. The referenced `docs/11-implementation-integration-specification.md` section
3. Every file in "Files to modify" — read the FULL file or at minimum the surrounding 100 lines of each modification point

## Step 3: Plan Presentation

Before writing code, present:
- What files you will create or modify
- For each modification: the exact function/section and what changes
- Which acceptance criteria you can verify and which you cannot
- Any questions or ambiguities

Wait for user confirmation before proceeding.

## Step 4: Implementation

- Create new files first, then modify existing files
- Each existing file modification: show the before/after context
- Feature-gate every behavioral change
- Match existing code style exactly

## Step 5: Verification Checklist

After implementation, explicitly check each acceptance criterion:
- [ ] List each criterion from the ticket
- [ ] Mark pass/fail/cannot-verify for each
- [ ] Flag any that need manual verification

If any criterion fails, fix it before declaring the ticket complete.
